Z||000000||GodSend||09-13-2000||02:21 PM||||  This weekend is EGR tube checking weekend.  Ive read more then a few descriptions of where to find the EGR tube (finding the egr is easy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> - <P>  I would like to ask a big favor of one of our members - Could someone draw the location/path of the EGR tube on the attached photo (compliments of the gallery) in bright yellow? - So people like me are sure they are checking the right tube?... thanks a million guys..<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/cruise.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by GodSend (edited 09-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||09-13-2000||03:45 PM||||It's hard to see in this picture.. it should be here, under all the stuff..<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cruise1.jpg"> <P>It goes from the EGR valve to under the plenum.  Corrugated tube covered with what used to be shiny silver insulation<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
